  "reasoning": "Octopuses possess three hearts and blue blood. Two branchial hearts pump blood through the gills, while a third systemic heart pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of the body. Their blood is blue because it uses a copper-rich protein called hemocyanin to bind and transport oxygen, rather than the iron-based hemoglobin found in vertebrates. When oxygenated, hemocyanin turns a distinct blue color.",
